{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Durable Memory Selection.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Durable Memory Selection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"durable memory selection durable memory selection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Durable Memory Selection.md","fileName":"Durable Memory Selection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Durable Memory Selection","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps Agent Memory and MCP]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Memory and MCP","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Durable Memory Selection.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Durable Memory Selection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"durable memory selection durable memory selection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Durable Memory Selection.md","fileName":"Durable Memory Selection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Durable Memory Selection","heading":"Durable Memory Selection","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Durable agent memory should contain concise, reusable, validated information such as repository conventions, deployment procedures, workflow progress, event outcomes, or references to approved observability summaries. It should not become a copy of every log or model response.\n\nSecrets, credentials, personal data, private reasoning, and unverified outputs are unsafe memory. A hallucination that is stored as long-term knowledge can contaminate later decisions. Selection therefore asks not only whether information might be useful, but whether its source, accuracy, sensitivity, scope, and future influence are acceptable.","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Memory and MCP","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32"